<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">M. C. Ricklefs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943–2019</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Merle Calvin Ricklefs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">M. C. Ricklefs was an American-born Australian historian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> who taught at Monash University, the Australian National University and the National University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>. His A History of Modern Indonesia since c. 1200 became a standard survey. In studies of Javanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> he described the court culture of Mataram as a 'mystic synthesis' of Islamic identity and Javanese spiritual traditions.</p></div>
